#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# associate_to

#% text
# `associate_to(a, rules)` adds the rules to the association held by the symbol `a`, stores the result back in `a` and gives it.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `rules` is a rule, a list of rules or an association; a key already present takes the new value.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
a = assoc(x -> 1, y -> 2)

#% cell
associate_to(a, x -> 10)
#% output
#= assoc(x -> 10, y -> 2)

#% cell
associate_to(a, [z -> 3])
#% output
#= assoc(x -> 10, y -> 2, z -> 3)

#% cell
a
#% output
#= assoc(x -> 10, y -> 2, z -> 3)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_drop_from`, `join`, `assoc`
